			<div class="content" id="post-content-4835559">
									

<p>Ok I am limited by 400 words and it's kinda hard to get everything across, but I mean that it isn't a single item that changes depending on what people think it is, and is whatever that is closest to it. It's an exact copy of what one person thinks it is, and can be more than one thing. Using the explosion example, someone can think it is just a folding chair, they can sit in that chair, and appears sitting on nothing, and someone who doesn't think it's a chair won't feel the chair/can't sit on it, but imagine that person thinks it's an explosive. Now they can move that explosive, and the chair the other person see doesn't move, the SCP is now 2 objects, while stilling being one SCP, and not SCP-1/A/whatever, both are just the &quot;standard&quot; SCP. OK so now that explosive is set off, and explodes, because the explosion would have the same effects as a normal one, the chair isn't moved, but there is still damage to the room and the other person, who thinks it's a chair. The reason for redactions is for people to think it's something harmless so it can't do something, and if someone thinks it's something that lives and just naturally destroys things, like a Keter that can easily escape it's room that can also cause massive damage. Only qualification is that someone has to think something that is it's name (SCP number) to be physical to only that person.</p>
<p>tl;dr - It takes only one person to change the scp, creating another thing which only is physical to that person, and scp can harm things and affect inanimate objects, and other people indirectly.</p>
<p>Just tell me if you think anything seems wrong, again I don't think I can get the <em>exact</em> thought in my head across.</p>

